0b104\u00c2\u00b1060302\u00c2\u00b1]MOE.model> but was:<0302-0601-3[\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1F06\u00ef\u00be\u00b1W220\u00ef\u00be\u00b1ZB\u00ef\u00be\u00b1LALALA\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1CAN\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1DC\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b1\u00ef\u00be\u00b104\u00ef\u00be\u00b1060302\u00ef\u00be\u00b1]MOE.model>\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.compress.archivers.tar.TarUtils\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: TarUtils.parseName does not properly handle characters outside the range 0-127\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nif a tarfile contains files with special characters, the names of the tar entries are wrong.\n\nexample:\ncorrect name: 0302-0601-3\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1F06\u00b1W220\u00b1ZB\u00b1LALALA\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1\u00b1CAN\u00b1\u00b1DC\u00b1\u00b1\u00b104\u00b1060302\u00b1MOE.model\nname resolved by TarUtils.parseName: 0302-0101-3\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1F06\uffb1W220\uffb1ZB\uffb1HECKMODUL\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1\uffb1ECE\uffb1\uffb1DC\uffb1\uffb1\uffb107\uffb1060302\uffb1DOERN.model\n\nplease use: \nresult.append(new String(new byte[] { buffer[i] }));\n\ninstead of: \nresult.append((char) buffer[i]);\n\nto solve this encoding problem.\n\nComments:\n\n[Sebb]: Could you provide a small sample tar file containing some files with the special names?\n[Perhaps the file contents could be the expected name]\n\nWe can then add the file to the test cases.\n\nThanks!\n\n[Sebb]: Forgot to mention:\n\nThe \"String(byte[])\" constructor depends on the default charset encoding, which might not always be what is wanted.\n\n[Helmut Minst]: tarfile which includes such files with a filename containing special characters\n\n[Helmut Minst]: that's right, but the cast from byte to char is not a beautiful way.\n\nString charsetName = \"ISO-8859-1\";\n                try {\n                    result.append(new String(new byte[] { buffer[i] }, charsetName));\n                } catch (UnsupportedEncodingException e) {\n                    result.append(new String(new byte[] { buffer[i] }));\n                }\n\nwhere charsetName may be set via a system property or sth else by the customer of commons compress.\n\n[Helmut Minst]: example where charset may be set by a setter in TarArchiveInpustream.\nif an UnsupportedEncodingException occurs, the default charset of the system\nis used.\n\nPlease have a look. Hope this helps to solve the problem.",
